# Ownership and required review.
#
# abulkheir is a personal account, so there are no teams — owners are named as
# individual usernames. Every name here must be a repository COLLABORATOR with at
# least write access, or GitHub ignores it silently and the rule does nothing.
#
# Inert until branch protection on `main` has "Require review from Code Owners"
# switched on. Without that, this file is documentation.
#
# IMPORTANT, and easy to get wrong: when a line lists several owners, GitHub is
# satisfied by an approval from ANY ONE of them. Only one rule applies to a file —
# the last one that matches — so a second line for the same path does not add a
# second requirement. CODEOWNERS therefore cannot express "the backend lead AND the
# PO must both approve". That is what .github/workflows/dual-approval.yml is for.

# The contract belongs to both reviewers. Neither may change it alone.
/contract/            @abyulkheir @abulkheirPO

# The source of truth and the record of what we assumed in its absence.
/backlog/             @abulkheirPO
/brd/                 @abulkheirPO
/assumptions/         @abulkheirPO

# The rules the process itself runs on.
/tools/               @abyulkheir @abulkheirPO
/docs/                @abulkheirPO
/.github/             @abyulkheir @abulkheirPO
